      <h2>Pitco at a glance, J.C. Pitman 1918, Frialator 1959 invention, Middleby family today</h2>
      <p>
        J.C. Pitman founded the company in 1918, manufacturing commercial fryers from New Hampshire. The Pitco
        Frialator was invented and patented in 1959 — that 1959 design became the brand's signature product
        architecture, and the "Pitco Frialator" name persists today as the active trade naming. Social-media
        handles read @pitcofrialator on Facebook and Instagram, @pitco_frialator on X. Manufacturing operates
        from Bow, New Hampshire (primary, decades-long) and Concord, New Hampshire (2021 expansion announced
        in the Concord Monitor).
      </p>
      <p>
