        chain runs through Blodgett — Blodgett Co. acquired Pitco in 1981, and Middleby acquired Blodgett in
        the early 2000s, bringing Pitco into the Middleby Corporation family where it has remained ever since.
        Middleby's website lists Pitco alongside sibling brands Ultrafryer and Anets (fryers), Blodgett (ovens),
        Southbend (ranges), Imperial Commercial Cooking, Viking Commercial, TurboChef rapid-cook, and several
        warming and holding brands. <b>Pitco is NOT Welbilt and NOT Ali Group</b> — that confusion shows up in
        older SERP content but is structurally wrong. Welbilt's foodservice portfolio (Frymaster, Garland,
        Lincoln, Manitowoc, Convotherm, Merrychef, Kolpak) moved to Ali Group in July 2022, but Pitco was never
        in that portfolio and has been Middleby family for roughly two decades.
      </p>
      <p>
